From: Animesh Kumar <animesh.kcm@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] security: escape SQLCipher PRAGMA key to prevent SQL injection via env var

The SQLCipher PRAGMA key is built with an f-string. If DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY
contains a single quote, the statement breaks. Escape the value by doubling
embedded quotes before interpolation. This is the canonical SQLite escape
because PRAGMA does not accept ? placeholders.

Reported in improvements/security-review.md#sec-01.

---
 src/database/connection.py | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/database/connection.py b/src/database/connection.py
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/src/database/connection.py
+++ b/src/database/connection.py
@@ -24,10 +24,11 @@ def get_engine(db_path: str, encryption_key: str | None = None) -> Engine:
     if encryption_key and os.environ.get("DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY"):
         try:

             @event.listens_for(engine, "connect")
             def set_sqlite_pragma(dbapi_conn, connection_record):
                 cursor = dbapi_conn.cursor()
-                cursor.execute(f"PRAGMA key='{encryption_key}'")
+                safe_key = encryption_key.replace("'", "''")
+                cursor.execute(f"PRAGMA key='{safe_key}'")
                 cursor.close()

         except Exception:
             pass  # Fall back to unencrypted SQLite
